{"title":"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(nonrigorous_+_abusing_answer_choices.)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (nonrigorous + abusing answer choices.)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(super_quick)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (super quick)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_7_(Not_rigorous_but_it_works)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7 (Not rigorous but it works)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Solution_8_(Assumption)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 8 (Assumption)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#=_Solution_9_(i_just_lost_my_dawg)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">= Solution 9 (i just lost my dawg)</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/9/8d96d19c649204cdd9c0ac3758e9555d73f6d7f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\log (2013 + \\log (2012 + \\log (2011 + \\log (\\cdots + \\log (3 + \\log 2) \\cdots ))))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"537\" height=\"18\" />. Which of the following intervals contains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/6/106c2fb8d6bd19573d0dd94f6a9ec2c7a7c8cf8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)} \\ (\\log 2016, \\log 2017)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"185\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/4/35410473cfbb7dda7fbfb8b549fe2ea4e9c941e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B)} \\ (\\log 2017, \\log 2018)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"180\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/d/b7dc1c446b8102eaca3632ebe60ae9ce1904a7a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(C)} \\ (\\log 2018, \\log 2019)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"180\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/e/bee0688e7867114726fa6394eda50ef530d35e96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)} \\ (\\log 2019, \\log 2020)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"181\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/2/c82c281ed6cc6d2068b049d376385c3670490041.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E)} \\ (\\log 2020, \\log 2021)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"179\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/f/e1fd583416410ac0a70373863e27c239cb9be162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = \\log(x + f(x-1))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"195\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f503e82227d1f7d6a63ed4db689463d0b2dcaaf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2) = \\log(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" />, and from the problem description, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/7/7779635fe30327e23b8bc2184f4706574c6c29ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = f(2013)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>We can reason out an approximation, by ignoring the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/e/93e72384515cd2cabbfbc86b20e6003fa1991f77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/e/00e1d3534f6acfbff50fd508d65802ee426d6807.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_{0}(x) \\approx \\log x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>And a better approximation, by plugging in our first approximation for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/e/93e72384515cd2cabbfbc86b20e6003fa1991f77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" /> in our original definition for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/3/633a37541a3bc635c55ac9a308805cb3694e5b16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_{1}(x) \\approx \\log(x + \\log(x-1))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"213\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>And an even better approximation:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/8/2e833f63eb51e5bc215131cfd8b7d03f73d45af8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_{2}(x) \\approx \\log(x + \\log(x-1 + \\log(x-2)))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"314\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Continuing this pattern, obviously, will eventually terminate at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/3/9f39266f89525a95ae7688f8d29a417a1023ca43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_{x-1}(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" />, in other words our original definition of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>However, at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/9/8991dcc3fdd9c5a926e18af4a07c1996c043dcef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 2013$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, going further than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/e/11ef5766b0426af45297faae19e02b472a57a59b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_{1}(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"18\" /> will not distinguish between our answer choices. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/8/ee86b3babfd331e069fe640a5f92277c5deedb21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log(2012 + \\log(2011))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"168\" height=\"18\" /> is nearly indistinguishable from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/7/747a5dc5c5ebbb41aa52e33cd37d7149620410d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log(2012)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>So we take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/e/11ef5766b0426af45297faae19e02b472a57a59b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_{1}(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"18\" /> and plug in.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/6/c761bf2ed343c09f5fbf0cb3d07ccbd825f4c39c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2013) \\approx \\log(2013 + \\log 2012)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"243\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/3/423e44751297b57170ec1e0fe9f51da5f1447f65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000 &lt; 2012 &lt; 10000$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"165\" height=\"13\" />, we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/0/75019e1b9433ab60e54664285d96984caaf85192.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 &lt; \\log(2012) &lt; 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"140\" height=\"18\" />. This gives us our answer range:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/a/deabd22e2ecfc30317784d0239862095b2c88333.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log 2016 &lt; \\log(2013 + \\log 2012) &lt; \\log(2017)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"342\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/8/088fd7e500107a7e80eca68ccc795edf9ea263a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\log 2016, \\log 2017)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/8/a783b06860ef4470d40cef90c0c7f4498b451df2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=\\log(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"88\" height=\"20\" />. \nThen <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/3/d7382a0abccfd4bcc9f109dcd404c4260de42b81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log(2012+ \\cdots)=x-2013$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"213\" height=\"18\" />. \nSo if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/a/c3a4827804f453a51aa85b2e1c13e9dfd38e261d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;2017$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/e/e8e5b8365b8026db543cbbda77efcf34cfcd8de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log(2012+\\log(2011+\\cdots))&gt;4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"250\" height=\"18\" />. \nSo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/c/8cce11a90091631b4de3507f0644362c23eb1696.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2012+\\log(2011+\\cdots)&gt;10000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"248\" height=\"18\" />. \nRepeating, we then get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/0/7e0814be5c665db29be7144cfe8f66587003bc65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2011+\\log(2010+\\cdots)&gt;10^{7988}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"247\" height=\"19\" />. \nThis is clearly absurd (the RHS continues to grow more than exponentially for each iteration).\nSo, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is not greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/1/5617f6d8def6056c5921630439d64b56cfa519ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2017$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" />. \nSo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/1/871695ee434a51fc8a0c7f40499f043bf1dda6df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&lt;\\log(2017)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"18\" />. \nBut this leaves only one answer, so we are done.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f503e82227d1f7d6a63ed4db689463d0b2dcaaf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2) = \\log(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/d/fed31504cc561c2c5f92fb65c9315695de05a3ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) = \\log(n+f(n-1)), \\text{ for } n &gt; 2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"285\" height=\"18\" /> We are looking for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/7/507bb4f14eed821f84fb072d2cb46e80cd90c7f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2013)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" />. First we show\n</p><p><b>Lemma.</b> For any integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3b9b7a46559a729577c3ca04dd2d7e66de16b3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/4/fc4c4725864fbe17dc65a60b8a7d2d923821da1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &lt; 10^k-k$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/0/990e8a2ff203747bd68d7ce8942d9cc72af69c62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) &lt; k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><b>Proof.</b> First note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/d/e1d72baf5c184b3fd81129bbad2c81c79953b1ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2) &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/6/c566b18cd754b2ccaba3f7094aa4d9c4584f34d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&lt;10^k-k$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/a/27a0ded0f32c8ab00b2dca85e95af99a1ebcf215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+k&lt;10^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"92\" height=\"17\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/4/3b4bddadad74c1aee36047524fb242ff1c474c9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log(n+k)&lt; k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"18\" />. Suppose the claim is true for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bdca93962a2beaffc172ca394e04fe05bd74ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/6/b9660ae6ab9e6d0c986ff7cbbfc42f98c5ab3afa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) = \\log(n+f(n-1)) &lt; \\log(n + k) &lt; k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"337\" height=\"18\" />.  The Lemma is thus proved by induction.\n</p><p>Finally, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/e/64ea2183aa7d2cc54f3724e6408e937a8b599f3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2012 &lt; 10^4 - 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"117\" height=\"15\" /> so that the Lemma implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/c/06c8b67c8c9e0fdd5cb752d69363dae840c2ad9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2012) &lt; 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" />. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/9/9792600cd1a0f58acad08fc7855e7db4aa813383.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2013) = \\log(2013+f(2012)) &lt; \\log(2017)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"339\" height=\"18\" />, which leaves us with only one option <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/7/2c7ecab82e24e9e1be8a18e48867e1dadf56faa3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } (\\log 2016, \\log 2017)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"195\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f503e82227d1f7d6a63ed4db689463d0b2dcaaf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2) = \\log(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/d/fed31504cc561c2c5f92fb65c9315695de05a3ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) = \\log(n+f(n-1)), \\text{ for } n &gt; 2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"285\" height=\"18\" /> We start with a simple observation:\n</p><p><b>Lemma.</b> For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/9/1b9f4d2caa7fd50dba44bb8c13b061b9cf72f8f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y&gt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/b/0db3c98227093e6a5aa7f642ae85e6e5e3ffef8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log(x+\\log(y)) &lt; \\log(x)+\\log(y)=\\log(xy)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"339\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><b>Proof.</b> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/9/1b9f4d2caa7fd50dba44bb8c13b061b9cf72f8f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y&gt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"15\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3da95fddf45c1a0d0b3819bf6b5acc8e13c651d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy-x-y = (x-1)(y-1) - 1 &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"283\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/d/6ddef7f4c1c2be51c19b430fa4dfd71341e772da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy - x-\\log(y) &gt; xy - x - y &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"263\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/8/0e833a2f1f3b48074a564a19e2196acc6c63ace2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log(z+\\log(x+\\log(y))) &lt; \\log(x)+\\log(y)+\\log(z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"395\" height=\"18\" />, and so on. \n</p><p>Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/2/24202ad600b19e31eb42fa0628851a7adc08e16a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2010) &lt; \\log 2 + \\log 3 + \\cdots + \\log 2010 &lt; \\log 2010 + \\cdots + \\log 2010 &lt;  2009\\cdot 4 = 8036$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"666\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/7/82714602dc5d58f10cc107518758fa07ecfd7998.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2011) = \\log(2011+f(2010)) &lt; \\log(10047) &lt; 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"383\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/4/7e48c3139646bd2a23a006dba779f77fd7d7bf94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2012) = \\log(2012+f(2011)) &lt; \\log(2017) &lt; 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"374\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>Finally, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/f/ecf6bb7cbed1725a97944730043d3d91143b7814.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2013) = \\log(2013 + f(2012)) &lt; \\log(2017)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"339\" height=\"18\" />, which leaves us with only option <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/e/35e8ea2d16518197b5113002b8c0c7da6c311a3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"41\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_5_.28nonrigorous_.2B_abusing_answer_choices..29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(nonrigorous_+_abusing_answer_choices.)\">Solution 5 (nonrigorous + abusing answer choices.)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (nonrigorous + abusing answer choices.)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Intuitively, you can notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/f/5bf2679cab6a7ba0a78e354e14e6af697c187c18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log(2012+\\log(2011+\\cdots(\\log(2)\\cdots))&lt;\\log(2013+\\log(2012+\\cdots(\\log(2))\\cdots))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"625\" height=\"18\" />, therefore (by the answer choices) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/b/7fbe251b53bbc4fc94a0a420f4a93d835c7d9e04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log(2012+\\log(2011+\\cdots(\\log(2)\\cdots))&lt;\\log(2021)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"394\" height=\"18\" />. We can then say:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/d/38d4771fec9e7ee63c679d1086eb9ab00d37876c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x=\\log(2013+\\log(2012+\\cdots(\\log(2))\\cdots))\\]\" width=\"337\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/1/7e1aa5de62850e57c0f09a30ad9435aaee44c2a4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log(2013)&lt;x&lt;\\log(2013+\\log(2021))\\]\" width=\"300\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/1/711751ba2126ea37114a3f48761218eed9d09f87.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log(2013)&lt;x&lt;\\log(2013+4)\\]\" width=\"236\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/1/5818fd64c02247a30223aa9098ccca3dd61046d7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log(2013)&lt;x&lt;\\log(2017)\\]\" width=\"204\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>The only answer choice that is possible given this information is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/e/35e8ea2d16518197b5113002b8c0c7da6c311a3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"41\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_6_.28super_quick.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(super_quick)\">Solution 6 (super quick)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (super quick)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/0/cc00b0335fad7558140f46eb1ec673654c98a6f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = \\log(x + \\log((x-1) + \\log((x-2) + \\ldots + \\log 2 \\ldots )))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"466\" height=\"20\" />. From the answer choices, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/d/6cdc3cd554120a289d8f1c888bc58cd5e2d6950e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 &lt; f(2013) &lt; 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"130\" height=\"20\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> grows very slowly, we can assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/c/f0c076ad0802dfe7054f420f094f8cd2c76e5cd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 &lt; f(2012) &lt; 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"130\" height=\"20\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78d069ac46d58e76ee41786f7818de706ccc87e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2013) = \\log(2013 + f(2012)) \\in (\\log 2016, \\log 2017) \\implies \\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"505\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~rayfish\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_7_.28Not_rigorous_but_it_works.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7_(Not_rigorous_but_it_works)\">Solution 7 (Not rigorous but it works)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7 (Not rigorous but it works)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Start small from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/8/db8115a334bac890e5a9615bb4edd77d022d5378.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log(3+\\log2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"106\" height=\"20\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/6/366f4f43bf856d820ddda1e32e374fe1468a30de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" /> is close to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the expression is close to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/2/6a23c2dcabcb3c1009b79e0e79bbd8fbe2309bdd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" />. This continues for the 1 digit numbers. However, when we get to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/6/e5643a402da512ac3c86b45795ed102f73b7613b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log(11+\\log10)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"125\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/d/e3d30d9f12ece703fa8e6f0701b93dd326e9b9d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log10=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" /> so the expression equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/d/29d7ee8d31c5353258959c6b56823a9e8914e2c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"18\" />. We can round down how much each new log contributes to the expression as an approximate answer. There are 90 2 digit numbers, 900 3 digit numbers, and 1014 4 digit numbers that increase the expression. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/7/8b747c7401ac1224cf07ed426e06b82333d70fa1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000&lt; 90 \\cdot 1 + 900 \\cdot 2 + 1014 \\cdot 3&lt; 10000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"325\" height=\"15\" />, so it increases between 3 and 4. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/e/35e8ea2d16518197b5113002b8c0c7da6c311a3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"41\" height=\"28\" />. \n</p><p>~dragnin\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_8_.28Assumption.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_8_(Assumption)\">Solution 8 (Assumption)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 8 (Assumption)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/8/f18008e7ef2634e7bf7031e3f347e023b5294bc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log (2013+\\log(2012))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"172\" height=\"20\" /> and disregard every other log. We do this because we assume that the logs from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/e/efe8f67ac18da14c8aa767b8131b0650ac9b9720.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2011$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> onward cannot contribute more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/4/e0411a567a409ac91997faefa8c3cd1447bbc25a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7987$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> because of the nature of logs. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/2/d62d61fb5871b90699e61d7a255e873dbb1685c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log(2016)&lt;\\log (2013+\\log(2012))&lt;\\log(2017)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"368\" height=\"20\" /> so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/4/3e49bd8afdebb1de3d873a06b57b95557e3f0cf1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{A}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"28\" height=\"24\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\".3D_Solution_9_.28i_just_lost_my_dawg.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"=_Solution_9_(i_just_lost_my_dawg)\">= Solution 9 (i just lost my dawg)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: = Solution 9 (i just lost my dawg)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>It seems that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/9/5b9484ae033c65fb0814bd452772005c396c69ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log (2012+x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"108\" height=\"20\" /> is going to be less than four, since otherwise, it would imply that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/3/833712e9623e6823222e0cb9cc5738925fcb931b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;7987$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"73\" height=\"15\" />, and going down, that seems very impossible.\n</p><p>Then, the answer is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/7/807989ef9121bc44b8beda0a826d5eeb770e3e9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{A} (\\log{2016}, \\log{2017})}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"176\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>Note: This solution is only for people with unlimited aura. (And veryyy limited time)\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/videos/amc/2013amc12a/360\">https://artofproblemsolving.com/videos/amc/2013amc12a/360</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A\">2013 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">